s_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.7-dev3, 4.7-dev4 and 4.7-dev5\n- Not reproducible in: 4.7-dev2 and earlier\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev3 - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Thu, 02 Apr 2026 23:33:01 +0000 on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon RX 570 Series (radeonsi, polaris10, ACO, DRM 3.64, 6.19.11-arch1-1) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-3770 CPU @ 3.40GHz (8 threads) - 31.29 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nRasterized text using a FontVariation isn't rendered correctly when the FontVariation's `transform` is slanted. It looks to me as if it it's being drawn with the transform's `yx` doubled and the `xy` inverted, somehow. It doesn't affect FontVariations with an MSDF font or text outlines (neither the ones from the `Label` node or from the `CanvasItem.draw_string_outline` method).\n\nHow it looks right now:\n<img width=\"1411\" height=\"834\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b1a0526d-1543-422b-8648-8ba71aca4fea\" />\n\nHow it's supposed to look:\n<img width=\"1389\" height=\"745\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8af06d52-d61b-4a49-a831-20a876809d3b\" />\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOn a new project, add a Label node, give it an outline, change its font to a FontVariation (theme override or thru LabelSettings, it doesn't matter) and slant the FontVariation using its transform's `yx` and `xy` fields.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[text bug mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26862998/text.bug.mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https: